---
title: Cranberry-Walnut Brussels Sprouts
servings: 4
prepTime: 10 min
cookTime: 20 min
$ating: 8/10
Description: Good reviews from Dudzek Christmas 2023. Even a 2# batch only took 20min to cook after prep work.
source: https://www.tasteofhome.com/recipes/cranberry-walnut-brussels-sprouts/
tags: Sides, Vegetables
---

In a #large skillet{}, heat @olive oil{1/4%cup} over medium heat.
Place @Brussels sprouts{1%pound}(fresh, trimmed and halved lengthwise) in pan, cut side down.
Cook ~{4-5%minutes} or until bottoms are browned.

Add @dried cranberries{1/2%cup} and @water{2%tbsp}.
Cook, covered, until Brussels sprouts are crisp-tender, 1-2 minutes.

Stir in @chopped walnuts{1/3%cup}; cook and stir until water is evaporated. 
Stir in @balsamic vinegar{2%tbsp}.

= Nutritional Information (per serving) =
281 calories, 20g fat (3g saturated fat), 0 cholesterol, 26mg sodium, 25g carbohydrate (14g sugars, 5g fiber), 5g protein
